Staging Layer Documentation

1. Purpose of the Staging Layer
The staging database represents the first landing zone for data extracted from OLTP source systems into the data warehouse environment. It is designed to temporarily store raw, source-aligned data with minimal to no transformation.
The staging layer serves as a buffer between operational systems and the Data Warehouse (DWH), ensuring data stability, auditability, and controlled ETL processing.
________________________________________
2. Design Principles
The staging layer follows these core principles:
•	Source-aligned structure: Tables closely resemble OLTP tables.
•	No business logic: No joins, aggregations, or calculations.
•	No constraints: No PKs, FKs, or indexes to allow fast bulk loads.
•	Auditability: Every record is traceable to a load batch and source.
•	Re-runnable ETL: Data can be reprocessed without touching OLTP.
________________________________________
3. Common Audit & Control Columns
Every staging table includes the following columns:
Column Name	Purpose
LoadDate	Timestamp when the record was loaded into staging
BatchID	Identifies the ETL batch/run for recovery and tracking
SourceSystem	Identifies the originating source system
These columns are mandatory for enterprise-grade ETL monitoring and troubleshooting.
