11. What the Staging Layer Is NOT Used For
•	No reporting or analytics
•	No business rule enforcement
•	No historical tracking logic (handled in DWH)
•	No aggregations or joins
________________________________________
12. Architectural Importance
The staging layer:
•	Protects OLTP systems from repeated ETL queries
•	Enables restartable and auditable ETL pipelines
•	Isolates bad or partial loads
•	Acts as a contractual boundary between source systems and the DWH
In enterprise BI architectures, direct loading from OLTP to DWH is avoided in favor of a staging layer for reliability, scalability, and governance.

